 accessible name. */\n.card__link {\n  color: inherit;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  outline-offset: 4px;\n}\n.card__link::after {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  border-radius: inherit;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n/* Anything that must stay clickable inside a stretched-link card. */\n.card__above { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\n50:[\"$\",\"$L4a\",\"Platform operations\",{\"as\":\"li\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-card\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$98\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"card card--pad-lg sv-card\",\"data-interactive\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-h3\",\"children\":\"Platform operations\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-card__line\",\"children\":\"We operate your SIEM and EDR — Wazuh, Elastic, Microsoft Sentinel, CrowdStrike, SentinelOne — or run ours. Your data stays in your tenancy and your region.\"}]]}]]}]\n99:T43d,\n.card {\n  position: relative;\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  color: inherit;\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.card--pad { padding: var(--s6); }\n.card--pad-lg { padding: var(--s8); }\n.card--flush { background-color: transparent; }\n\n/* Hover: colour only. Anything that moves the card is a spec violation. */\n.card[data-interactive='true']:hover,\n.card:has(.card__link):hover,\n.card:has(.card__link:focus-visible) {\n  background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--surface) 88%, var(--fg) 12%);\n  border-color: var(--border-strong);\n}\n\n/* The stretched link. The anchor's own text stays the accessible name. */\n.card__link {\n  color: inherit;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  outline-offset: 4px;\n}\n.card__link::after {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  border-radius: inherit;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n/* Anything that must stay clickable inside a stretched-link card. */\n.card__above { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\n51:[\"$\",\"$L4a\",\"Coverage reporting\",{\"as\":\"li\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-card\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$99\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"card card--pad-lg sv-card\",\"data-interactive\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-h3\",\"children\":\"Coverage reporting\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-card__line\",\"children\":\"Monthly ATT&CK coverage, detection changes, alert volume, false-positive rate and tuning decisions, with the reasoning.\"}]]}]]}]\n53:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"dg\",\"id\":\"engagement-shape\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-gantt\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 252\",\"preserveAspectRatio\":\"xMidYMid meet\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"Engagement shape for Managed Detection & Response: 6 phases. Phase 1, Architecture onboarding, Weeks 1–2, inside the engagement window. Phase 2, Telemetry and baseline, Weeks 2–4, inside the engagement window. Phase 3, Detection build, Weeks 4–6, inside the engagement window, producing the detection repository, version-controlled, mapped to mitre att&ck, yours to keep. Phase 4, Runbook and authority, Week 6, inside the engagement window, producing the incident runbook with agreed containment authority and escalation paths. Phase 5, Go live, Week 7, inside the engagement window. Phase 6, Operate and improve, Ongoing, no fixed window.\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-axisUnit\",\"x\":0,\"y\":16,\"children\":\"weeks from kick-off\"}],[[\"$\",\"g\",\"0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":236,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":236,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":236,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":0}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":379.42857142857144,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":379.42857142857144,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":379.42857142857144,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":2}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":522.8571428571429,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":522.8571428571429,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":522.8571428571429,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":4}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"6\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":666.2857142857142,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":666.2857142857142,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":666.2857142857142,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":6}]]}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-zero\",\"x1\":236,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":236,\"y2\":232}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-zeroLabel\",\"x\":236,\"y\":245,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":\"kick-off\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-colHead\",\"x\":762,\"y\":16,\"children\":\"Drops out\"}],[[\"$\",\"g\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":65,\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":65,\"children\":\"Architecture onboarding\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":236,\"y\":53.5,\"width\":143.42857142857144,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":387.42857142857144,\"y\":64,\"children\":\"Weeks 1–2\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":64,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":95,\"children\":\"02\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":95,\"children\":\"Telemetry and baseline\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":307.7142857142857,\"y\":83.5,\"width\":215.14285714285717,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":530.8571428571429,\"y\":94,\"children\":\"Weeks 2–4\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":94,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":125,\"children\":\"03\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":125,\"children\":\"Detection build\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":451.1428571428571,\"y\":113.5,\"width\":215.1428571428571,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":674.2857142857142,\"y\":124,\"children\":\"Weeks 4–6\"}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-leader\",\"x1\":748,\"y1\":121,\"x2\":757,\"y2\":121}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artMark\",\"x\":757,\"y\":117,\"width\":8,\"height\":8,\"rx\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-art\",\"x\":771,\"y\":124,\"children\":\"Detection repository, version…\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":155,\"children\":\"04\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":155,\"children\":\"Runbook and authority\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":594.5714285714286,\"y\":143.5,\"width\":71.71428571428567,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":674.2857142857142,\"y\":154,\"children\":\"Week 6\"}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-leader\",\"x1\":748,\"y1\":151,\"x2\":757,\"y2\":151}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artMark\",\"x\":757,\"y\":147,\"width\":8,\"height\":8,\"rx\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-art\",\"x\":771,\"y\":154,\"children\":\"Incident runbook with agreed…\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"5\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":185,\"children\":\"05\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":185,\"children\":\"Go live\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":666.2857142857142,\"y\":173.5,\"width\":71.71428571428578,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":658.2857142857142,\"y\":184,\"textAnchor\":\"end\",\"children\":\"Week 7\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":184,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"6\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":215,\"children\":\"06\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":215,\"children\":\"Operate and improve\"}],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-standing\",\"x1\":236,\"y1\":211,\"x2\":738,\"y2\":211}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":242,\"y\":205,\"children\":\"Ongoing\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":214,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}]]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-ganttText\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sched\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"dg-schedRow\",\"data-stage\":\"window\",\"children\":[\"$L9a\",\"$L9b\",\"$L9c\",\"$L9d\"]}],\"$L9e\",\"$L9f\",\"$La0\",\"$La1\",\"$La2\"]}]}],\"$La3\"]}]\na4:Tc1d,\n/* ---- Chapter ------------------------------------------------------------\n   A numbered chapter with a heading that HOLDS while its body scrolls under\n   it. The number is not decoration: it tells a reader where they are in a long\n   page, which is the thing a long page actually owes them. */\n.ch {\n  position: relative;\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s8);\n}\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .ch {\n    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr);\n    gap: var(--s16);\n    align-items: start;\n  }\n}\n\n.ch__head {\n  position: relative;\n}\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .ch__head {\n    position: sticky;\n    /* Clears the fixed 72px nav plus breathing room. */\n    top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s8));\n  }\n}\n\n.ch__num {\n  display: block;\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  letter-spacing: 0.18em;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  margin-bottom: var(--s3);\n}\n\n.ch__title {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, var(--text-4xl));\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}\n\n.ch__lede {\n  margin: var(--s4) 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: var(--text-base);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  max-width: 34ch;\n}\n\n.ch__rule {\n  margin-top: var(--s6);\n  height: 1px;\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), transparent);\n}\n\n.ch__body {\n  min-width: 0;\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s12);\n}\n\n/* ---- Sticky card stack --------------------------------------------------\n   Every card is sticky at the SAME offset, so each comes to rest on the one\n   before it and the stack assembles itself as you scroll. The entire effect is\n   the equal `top` value — there is no JavaScript here at all.\n\n   Each card needs its own opaque background or the stack reads as a smear;\n   that is the one thing people get wrong when copying this. */\n.stack {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s8);\n}\n.stack__card {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s8));\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  padding: var(--s8);\n  /* A hairline of the ground above each card so stacked edges stay readable. */\n  box-shadow: 0 -1px 0 0 var(--bg);\n}\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .stack__card {\n    padding: var(--s12);\n  }\n}\n\n/* The stack is a scroll effect. Under reduced motion it is simply a list —\n   which is what it already is semantically, so nothing is lost. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .stack__card,\n  .ch__head {\n    position: static;\n  }\n}\n/* Sticky needs a real scroll context; without JS the layout is identical, so\n   no .no-js override is required here. */\n\n.stack__index {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  letter-spacing: 0.16em;\n  color: var(--accent);\n}\n.stack__title {\n  margin: var(--s3) 0 0;\n  font-size: var(--text-2xl);\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n}\n.stack__body {\n  margin: var(--s4) 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  line-height: 1.65;\n  max-width: 62ch;\n}\n\n@media print {\n  .stack__card,\n  .ch__head {\n    position: static;\n  }\n}\n54:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-phaseStack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-story\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$a4\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"stack\",\"children\":[\"$La5\",\"$La6\",\"$La7\",\"$La8\",\"$La9\",\"$Laa\"]}]]}]\nab:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n55:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-note\",\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"var(--s8)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-button\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$ab\"}],\"$Lac\"]}]\n57:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"dg dg-stackFig\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-stack\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 531 358\",\"preserveAspectRatio\":\"xMidYMin meet\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"What lands in your inbox on a Managed Detection & Response engagement: 6 deliverables. 1, Detection repository, version-controlled, mapped to MITRE ATT&CK, yours to keep, in your repo. 2, Validated log source inventory with coverage gaps named, written document. 3, Incident runbook with agreed containment authority and escalation paths, operating doc. 4, Monthly coverage and tuning report with reasoning, not just counts, written report. 5, Quarterly purple-team validation of the detections that matter, written document. 6, Post-incident reports with root cause and control changes, written report.\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"g\",\"Detection repository, version-controlled, mapped to MITRE ATT&CK, yours to keep\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheet\",\"x\":18,\"y\":18,\"width\":470,\"height\":92,\"rx\":6}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetSpine\",\"x\":18,\"y\":18,\"width\":3,\"height\":92}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetNum u-mono\",\"x\":36,\"y\":38,\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",nu